<title>USA: Missouri jobless rate rises to 5 pct in January.</title>
<headline>Missouri jobless rate rises to 5 pct in January.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Missouri's unemployment rate rose to five percent in January from 4.7 percent in December, according to the state's department of labor and industrial relations.</p>
<p>The department, which attributed the increase partly to winter weather and the end of the holiday retail season, estimated that 142,100 workers were without jobs in January, up by 5,300 from December.</p>
<p>The percentage of jobless workers in January was lower than January 1996 when the unemployment rate stood at 5.1 percent.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
</text>
